# Computing in the Business Curriculum.

**Authors:** 

## Abstract
This catalog is a collection of computer programs which have been designed and used as curricular support in Business Education on the college level. It is intended for use by the business instructor who wishes to initiate the use of the computer as an instructional aid in his courses. Discipline areas covered include: (1) accounting, (2) finance, (3) management information systems, (4) management, (5) marketing, (6) quantitative methods, and (7) simulation models. Individual course descriptions and objectives, computer program descriptions and objectives, and program documentation are provided. (Author/STS)

